go 1.26.5

// Two modules, and deliberately no shared third one: the client and the
// server have no import edge between them, so neither needs a `replace`
// directive and each builds standalone without this file.
//
// This workspace exists only so that gopls treats both as one project — so
// go-to-definition, find-references and rename work across the boundary in a
// single editor window. It is committed because it is this repo's dev setup
// rather than a local override; the advice to gitignore go.work applies to
// libraries, where it would override a consumer's own workspace.
use (
	./client
	./server
)
